==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
Named after [[w:Hans Gerhard Creutzfeldt|Hans Gerhard Creutzfeldt]] and [[w:Alfons Maria Jakob|Alfons Maria Jakob]].

===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=Creutzfeldt-Jakob [[disease]]|-}}  (''abbreviation'' '''[[CJD]]''')

# {{disease|neurology}} A [[rare]], [[progressive]],  currently [[fatal]] [[disease]] of the [[nervous system]], characterized by [[dementia]] and loss of [[muscle]] [[control]]. A [[prion]] disease, apparently transmissible from animals to humans by eating infected tissue, as well as from tissue interchanges among humans (corneal transplants, blood transfusions).

